description:
Show a remote player smoothly from irregular snapshots by rendering a fixed delay in the past and blending between snapshots (lesson 6.03).

```cpp
struct Snapshot { double time; double x; double y; };

class Interpolator
{
public:
    Interpolator(double delay, double maxExtrapolation);
    void add(const Snapshot& s);
    std::optional<std::pair<double, double>> positionAt(double now) const;
    std::size_t buffered() const;
};
```

- **add** stores a snapshot unless its time is not newer than the newest one already stored (an out-of-order arrival), keeping at most the 32 newest.
- **positionAt** renders at `t = now - delay`:
  - with no snapshots, there is no position;
  - at or before the oldest snapshot, the oldest position;
  - between two stored snapshots, the straight-line blend of the two around `t`;
  - after the newest snapshot: with only one snapshot, its position; otherwise continue at the velocity between the two newest snapshots for `t - newest time`, but for no longer than `maxExtrapolation`, then hold there.
- **buffered** is the number of snapshots stored.

